terms.definition:
All contracts to be entered into by the Group (or a Group Company) for:
(a)	O&M contracts
(b)	grid connection agreements; 
(c)	wind turbines, including any initial period of service, supply and warranty agreements and material spare parts and tools supply agreements; 
(d)	turbine foundations or substantial portions thereof, such as monopiles, jackets, transition pieces, transport and/or installation services therefor;
(e)	export cables;
(f)	inter-array cables; 
(g)	electrical balance of plant;
(h)	onshore substations or substantial portions thereof, such as civil works or electrical works;
(i)	ownership of, or rights to use of the seabed, including leases, options and agreements for lease;
(j)	offshore substations or substantial portions thereof, such as foundations, topsides, electrical equipment or transport and installation services thereof; 
(k)	key transport and/or installation services, vessel charters and operations and maintenance vessel charters;
(l)	access and use of port facilities for the operation and construction phases, including real estate contracts; 
(m)	coordination between offshore windfarm projects;
(n)	cable crossing agreements;
(o)	the sale and purchase, trading and/or marketing of power (including renewable energy certificates, however described in the relevant jurisdiction) and any associated contracts or contracts for difference relating to the offtake of power, including any bid awards relating to the same;
(p)	any other contract designated as a Project Contract in a Business Plan (as approved by the Shareholders); or 
(q)	any other document entered into by a Group Company in connection with the ownership, development, construction, commissioning, testing, operation, maintenance, decommissioning and financing of a Project approved in a Business Plan (as approved by the Shareholders)

references.description:
Each Business Plan shall include the following:
(a)	a description of the Group’s strategy and strategic priorities;
(b)	a Work Plan of the Group; 
(c)	the Annual Budget;
(d)	a financial forecast of the Group for the next five years (the Forecast) containing the following (as a minimum): 
(i)	in respect of the Committed Projects (which have not been abandoned), a project by project financial forecast;
(ii)	in respect of the New Projects or Projects other than the Committed Projects a project by project financial forecast if, in relation to such New Project or Project the Group has committed or expects to commit greater than USD$25 million in total as part of the Annual Budget; and
(iii)	Group profit and loss account and cash flow statement; and
(e)	an indicative (and non-binding) financial forecast for the Group for five years following the end of the Forecast period, in the same form and containing similar details as is included in the Forecast;
(f)	the Financial Plan;
(g)	a list of Project Contracts (being those with an aggregate liability per contract of more than US$50 million), and details of the relevant counterparty or counterparties to such Project Contracts; and 
(h)	details of the actual or contingent commitments of the Group during the next two (2) year period, including those that are guaranteed under a Project Guarantee (and, if applicable, details of the tenor, quantum and beneficiary under such Project Guarantees), 
together with a description of the current status of the work programme and other activities in respect of each Project to which the Business Plan relates.
